    headline: "Every interaction has a status rhythm",
    why: "Status is not a possession, it is a negotiation conducted in real time through tiny moves: who speaks first, who fills silence, who explains, who apologises, who occupies space, whose joke gets laughed at. Because it is behavioural, it can be read — and once it can be read, it can be dialled deliberately rather than left on one setting.",
