    why: "Micro-expressions — the sub-quarter-second contractions that precede a managed face — are genuinely informative and genuinely dangerous. The information is real: something happened emotionally that was not intended to show. The danger is that a fraction of a second of data feels like proof, and people upgrade it to a conclusion within about two seconds.",
