    why: "A callback is the only joke whose setup has already been paid for. Because the room has already reacted to the earlier moment, a two-word reference can produce a disproportionate laugh — and, more importantly, it produces a *feeling of shared history*, which is worth more than the laugh. This is why inside jokes are the fastest social glue there is.",
